# Fenn — an old fisherman by the lake who wants perch for his stew. Format: dialogue/dialogue_parser.gd
@speaker Fenn
@when fenn_got_fish -> after
@when fenn_quest_accepted -> reminder

== offer ==
Quiet, quiet! You'll spook them. ...Too late. They've gone.
Forty years I've fished this lake, and today my back says [i]no[/i]. And I promised the whole street my famous perch stew.
You've got a rod arm, haven't you? Stand at the water's edge, face the lake, and cast your line. [whisper]Wait for the bobber to dip, then reel.[/whisper]
Three [color=#6fa84a]perch[/color] is all I need. Plump little green ones. Will you?
> Three perch. Easy. -> accepted [set fenn_quest_accepted]
> Not today. -> no

== no ==
Hmph. My stew pot is going to be very lonely.

== accepted ==
Ha! A friend of the fish! Mind you, the lake sends minnows first. Be patient, [wave]the perch come to those who wait[/wave].

== reminder ==
Got my three [color=#6fa84a]perch[/color] yet? Cast from the water's edge. Minnows don't count, I'm afraid.
> Here, three perch. -> thanks [item perch 3] [set fenn_got_fish]
> Still fishing.

== thanks ==
[bounce]Look at those beauties![/bounce] Plump as a mayor. The whole street will be at my door tonight.
Here, for your trouble. And a secret: they say a [color=#d9a21b]golden koi[/color] swims out there, once in a blue moon. [whisper]If you ever land it, keep it. Or sell it. Nobody'd blame you.[/whisper]

== after ==
Best stew in Chesburg, thanks to you. If you see a flash of gold in that lake, [i]you didn't hear it from me.[/i]
